---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="About Convera Strategies" description="About Convera Strategies, its perspective, purpose, and founder-led approach." canonical="/about/">
  <PageHero eyebrow="About Convera Strategies" title="Perspective for people, organizations, and institutions." lede="Convera Strategies is an independent, founder-led practice built around a simple premise: better decisions begin with a wider understanding of people, context, relationships, and institutional conditions." compact />

  <section class="section about-purpose" aria-labelledby="about-purpose-title">
    <div class="container about-purpose__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What Convera Is</p>
        <h2 id="about-purpose-title">A place for questions that do not fit neatly inside one discipline.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="about-purpose__copy">
        <p>Convera begins from the view that organizations and institutions are ultimately experienced through people, relationships, communication, expectations, and trust.</p>
        <p>Organizations rarely experience problems in isolation. Workplace culture, communication, public expectations, institutional history, social conditions, and leadership decisions often overlap.</p>
        <p>Convera brings those relationships into view. Its work combines social perspective, workplace understanding, organizational strategy, research, and careful observation without forcing every question into a predetermined consulting model.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section about-pillars" aria-labelledby="about-pillars-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">The Convera Perspective</p><h2 id="about-pillars-title">Three fields. One connected view.</h2></div>
      <div class="about-pillar-grid">
        <article class="card"><span>01</span><h3>Social Perspectives</h3><p>Look beyond the immediate issue to the institutional, community, cultural, and relational conditions surrounding it.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><span>02</span><h3>Workplace Culture</h3><p>Examine how people communicate, interpret expectations, build trust, and experience organizational life in practice.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><span>03</span><h3>Organizational Strategy</h3><p>Translate a clearer understanding of context into priorities, decisions, and practical next steps.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section about-context" aria-labelledby="about-context-title">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="about-context__heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Perspective in Practice</p><h2 id="about-context-title">People and systems are rarely separate.</h2></div>
        <p class="lede">Convera Strategies looks at both sides of organizational life: how people experience a setting and how structures, expectations, communication, and institutional practices shape that experience.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="about-context__visuals">
        <article class="about-visual-card card">
          <div class="about-visual-card__media"><img src="/images/editorial/convera-people-network.svg" alt="Abstract illustration representing people, relationships, and connection" width="1200" height="720" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="about-visual-card__copy"><p class="eyebrow">People & Relationships</p><h3>What people experience matters.</h3><p>Trust, communication, expectations, informal norms, and everyday interactions often reveal conditions that formal processes alone cannot explain.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="about-visual-card card">
          <div class="about-visual-card__media"><img src="/images/editorial/convera-institution-systems.svg" alt="Abstract illustration representing organizations, institutions, and connected systems" width="1200" height="720" loading="lazy" /></div>
          <div class="about-visual-card__copy"><p class="eyebrow">Institutions & Systems</p><h3>Structure shapes what becomes possible.</h3><p>Policies, roles, routines, records, incentives, and institutional history can strengthen good work or create friction around it.</p></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section about-method" id="convera-approach" aria-labelledby="about-method-title">
    <div class="container about-method__grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">The Convera Approach</p><h2 id="about-method-title">Similar problems may require different responses.</h2></div>
      <div class="about-method__copy">
        <p>Problems carrying the same label may arise from different organizational conditions, institutional histories, group relationships, and operational practices. Convera Strategies begins by examining these differences rather than assuming a standard diagnosis or response will apply.</p>
        <p>Each engagement starts with systematic problem definition. Relevant records, administrative data, policies, documented practices, stakeholder accounts, and existing research are examined within their organizational and institutional contexts.</p>
        <p>Theoretical analysis helps identify the explanations and assumptions guiding current practice. Philosophical inquiry is used more narrowly to clarify questions of purpose, responsibility, value, and consequence when those questions affect how the problem is defined or addressed.</p>
        <p>This integrated approach supports responses shaped by the actual conditions of the problem rather than by category alone.</p>
        <div class="about-method__steps" aria-label="Convera approach">
          <div><span>01</span><strong>Understand the current state.</strong><p>Listen first, establish context, and identify what is actually happening.</p></div>
          <div><span>02</span><strong>Preserve what is working.</strong><p>Separate genuine strengths from the conditions creating unnecessary friction.</p></div>
          <div><span>03</span><strong>Move in deliberate increments.</strong><p>Choose practical steps tied to the outcome rather than change for appearance alone.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section founder-bridge" aria-labelledby="founder-bridge-title">
    <div class="container founder-bridge__grid">
      <div class="founder-bridge__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Founder</p>
        <h2 id="founder-bridge-title">Meet Ryan Brown.</h2>
        <p class="founder-bridge__identity">{site.founderIdentity}</p>
        <p>Ryan’s path into this work spans service occupations, military and law-enforcement experience, academic research, teaching, public institutions, and professional roles centered on people and responsibility. His personal profile explores how those experiences shaped the questions, values, and vision behind Convera.</p>
        <div class="founder-bridge__actions"><a class="button button--primary" href="/profile/">View Ryan’s Profile →</a><a class="button button--ghost" href="/mission/">Read Convera’s Mission →</a></div>
      </div>
      <figure class="founder-bridge__portrait"><img src="/images/ryan-brown.jpg" alt="Ryan Brown, founder of Convera Strategies" width="1535" height="1024" loading="lazy" /></figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    .about-purpose__grid,.about-method__grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.82fr) minmax(0,1.18fr);gap:clamp(2rem,5vw,5rem);align-items:start}
    .about-purpose h2,.about-method h2{margin:.5rem 0 0}.about-purpose__copy,.about-method__copy{display:grid;gap:1rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:1.05rem}
    .about-pillars{background:var(--surface-soft);border-block:1px solid var(--line)}
    .about-pillar-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}
    .about-pillar-grid article{padding:1.45rem}.about-pillar-grid span{color:var(--accent);font-size:.7rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.16em}.about-pillar-grid h3{margin:.55rem 0 .7rem}.about-pillar-grid p{color:var(--muted);font-size:.94rem}
    .about-context__heading{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,.86fr) minmax(0,1.14fr);gap:clamp(2rem,5vw,5rem);align-items:end;margin-bottom:1.3rem}.about-context__heading h2{margin:.5rem 0 0}
    .about-context__visuals{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.about-visual-card{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(170px,.72fr) minmax(0,1.28fr);overflow:hidden}.about-visual-card__media{min-height:220px;background:var(--surface-soft)}.about-visual-card__media img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover}.about-visual-card__copy{align-self:center;padding:1.2rem 1.35rem}.about-visual-card__copy h3{margin:.45rem 0 .6rem;font-size:clamp(1.35rem,2vw,1.8rem)}.about-visual-card__copy p:not(.eyebrow){color:var(--muted);font-size:.93rem}
    .about-method{background:var(--bg);border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .about-method__steps{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.75rem;margin-top:.35rem}.about-method__steps>div{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--surface) 90%,transparent)}.about-method__steps span{display:block;margin-bottom:.35rem;color:var(--accent);font-size:.68rem;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.14em}.about-method__steps strong{display:block;color:var(--text);font-family:"Cormorant Garamond",Georgia,serif;font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:600;line-height:1.05}.about-method__steps p{margin-top:.45rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.45}
    .founder-bridge{padding-block:clamp(2rem,3.4vw,3rem);background:var(--surface-soft);border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.founder-bridge__grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(240px,310px);gap:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.4rem);align-items:center}.founder-bridge__copy h2{margin:.45rem 0 .35rem}.founder-bridge__identity{margin:0 0 .8rem;color:var(--accent);font-size:.72rem!important;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase}.founder-bridge__copy>p:not(.eyebrow):not(.founder-bridge__identity){max-width:52rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:1rem}.founder-bridge__actions{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.75rem;margin-top:1.1rem}.founder-bridge__portrait{margin:0;overflow:hidden;border-radius:12px;background:var(--surface)}.founder-bridge__portrait img{width:100%;height:230px;object-fit:cover;object-position:center 29%}
    @media(max-width:980px){.about-context__visuals{grid-template-columns:1fr}.about-method__steps{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
    @media(max-width:820px){.about-purpose__grid,.about-method__grid,.about-context__heading,.founder-bridge__grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.about-pillar-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.about-visual-card{grid-template-columns:1fr}.about-visual-card__media{min-height:180px}.founder-bridge__portrait{max-width:360px}.founder-bridge__portrait img{height:250px}}
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
